<title>CHILE: Chile' Andina raises stake in bottler.</title>
<headline>Chile' Andina raises stake in bottler.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean soft drinks bottler Embotelladora Andina SA said on Monday its unit Inversiones del Atlantico SA had bought a 5.1 percent stake in Argentina's Embotelladora del Atlantico, raising its participation to 99.99 percent.</p>
<p>Andina reported to Chile's Securities and Insurance Commission that it would pay $5.5 million for the stake.</p>
<p>The Argentine firm in turn controls Rosario Mendoza Refrescos SA, which bottles Coca-Cola Co drinks in Rosario and Mendoza, two of Argentina's main cities.</p>
<p>((Santiago newsroom, +562 699 5595 x 211))</p>
